# XSH sem_unlink()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Names are "/pcsem<pid><tag>" and are unlinked again on every exit path.
# EACCES (permission to unlink) cannot be arranged for a name that need
# not be in the file system and is not tested.

assertion  XSH.sem_unlink.001
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#ERRORS/ENOENT
class      required
says       sem_unlink() of an existing name returns 0; sem_open(name, 0)
           then fails with ENOENT, and a second sem_unlink() fails with
           ENOENT.
test       t/001-removes-name.c

assertion  XSH.sem_unlink.002
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#ERRORS/ENOENT
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       sem_unlink() of a name that never existed returns -1 with
           errno ENOENT.
test       t/002-enoent.c

assertion  XSH.sem_unlink.003
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       After sem_unlink() of a name whose semaphore is still open, the
           name can be created again with O_CREAT|O_EXCL; the new
           semaphore has the new value and is a different semaphore from
           the open one, which keeps its own.
test       t/003-name-reusable.c

assertion  XSH.sem_unlink.004
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       sem_unlink() has no effect on the state of the semaphore a handle
           is open to: sem_wait(), sem_post() and sem_timedwait() on that
           handle go on working with the right counts, and sem_close()
           of it returns 0.
test       t/004-open-handle-works.c

assertion  XSH.sem_unlink.005
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/sem_close.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       After sem_unlink() and the sem_close() of the only handle, the
           name is created again with O_CREAT|O_EXCL (no EEXIST) and the
           new semaphore has the new value, not the old one.
test       t/005-after-last-close.c

assertion  XSH.sem_unlink.006
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
says       sem_unlink() of a name while another process has the semaphore
           open returns 0 at once (it does not wait for that process), and
           the other process's open semaphore still holds its value
           afterwards.
timeout    90
test       t/006-other-process-holds.c

assertion  XSH.sem_unlink.007
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#ERRORS/ENAMETOOLONG
anchor     functions/sem_unlink.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       With a name of 5000 bytes: if sem_open() created it, sem_unlink()
           of the same name returns 0 (no ENAMETOOLONG for a name used in
           a successful sem_open()); if sem_open() refused it, sem_unlink()
           returns -1 with ENAMETOOLONG or ENOENT.
test       t/007-name-too-long.c
